{"authored" [{"question" "q-161490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{x}^{x+y}(y+2z)\\,dz]dA\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le x}.\n$$" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161490/review.json" "file_sha256" "2d616e8e0ec7b3fc52f4136f5135463d01e620bc3554d6a75d6965e1ff18bb6e" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161490/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "e9e2bd448aff49c5c2aa0e0047828362b6bb355c9992d197e169ee393dd926f4" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161490/verification.json" "basis" 2022 "rationale" "Correct only the isolated intermediate outer limits0→1 to the actual domain limits1→2. The integrand(5/3)x³ and value25/4 are correct; preserve prompt, source, all existing fields, answer identities, and correct key."} {"question" "q-161490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{x}^{x+y}(y+2z)\\,dz]dA & ={∬}_{D}[yz+{z}^{2}]_{z=x}^{z=x+y}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y((x+y)-x)+((x+y)^{2}-{x}^{2})\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}+2xy+{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}2xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}2xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[x{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x({x}^{2}-0)+\\frac{2}{3}({x}^{3}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{3}\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}(16-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161490/review.json" "file_sha256" "2d616e8e0ec7b3fc52f4136f5135463d01e620bc3554d6a75d6965e1ff18bb6e" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161490/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "e9e2bd448aff49c5c2aa0e0047828362b6bb355c9992d197e169ee393dd926f4" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161490/verification.json" "basis" 2022 "rationale" "Correct only the isolated intermediate outer limits0→1 to the actual domain limits1→2. The integrand(5/3)x³ and value25/4 are correct; preserve prompt, source, all existing fields, answer identities, and correct key."} {"question" "q-161490" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{25}{4}"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161490/review.json" "file_sha256" "2d616e8e0ec7b3fc52f4136f5135463d01e620bc3554d6a75d6965e1ff18bb6e" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161490/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "e9e2bd448aff49c5c2aa0e0047828362b6bb355c9992d197e169ee393dd926f4" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161490/verification.json" "basis" 2022 "rationale" "Correct only the isolated intermediate outer limits0→1 to the actual domain limits1→2. The integrand(5/3)x³ and value25/4 are correct; preserve prompt, source, all existing fields, answer identities, and correct key."} {"question" "q-161490" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{x}^{x+y}(y+2z)\\,dz]dA\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ 